ve models, software quality, Analytical models, Bayes methods, Context modeling, contextual information, cost reduction, Fault diagnosis, fault prediction models, fault prediction performance, fault prediction study, feature selection, independent variables, logistic regression, methodological information, naive Bayes, predictive performance, regression analysis, reliable methodology, simple modeling techniques, software engineering, software fault prediction, software fault tolerance, Software testing, systematic literature review, Systematic literature review, Systematics","pages":"1276--1304"},"diffs":[{"field":"year","in_document":"2012","in_source":"2011","severity":"medium"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"henderson-sellers_object-oriented_1996","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"address":"Upper Saddle River, NJ, USA","title":"Object-oriented {Metrics}: {Measures} of {Complexity}","isbn":"0-13-239872-9","publisher":"Prentice-Hall, Inc.","author":"Henderson-Sellers, Brian","year":"1996"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"jureczko_towards_2010","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"address":"New York, NY, USA","series":"{PROMISE} '10","title":"Towards {Identifying} {Software} {Project} {Clusters} with {Regard} to {Defect} {Prediction}","isbn":"978-1-4503-0404-7","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/1868328.1868342","doi":"10.1145/1868328.1868342","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 6th {International} {Conference} on {Predictive} {Models} in {Software} {Engineering}","publisher":"ACM","author":"Jureczko, Marian and Madeyski, Lech","year":"2010","keywords":"defect prediction, clustering, design metrics, size metrics","pages":"9:1--9:10"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"kamei_defect_2016-1","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"title":"Defect {Prediction}: {Accomplishments} and {Future} {Challenges}","volume":"5","doi":"10.1109/SANER.2016.56","booktitle":"2016 {IEEE} 23rd {International} {Conference} on {Software} {Analysis}, {Evolution}, and {Reengineering} ({SANER})","author":"Kamei, Y. and Shihab, E.","month":"mar","year":"2016","keywords":"Complexity theory, Data models, defect prediction, Market research, Power measurement, Predictive models, Software, software defect prediction, software metrics, software prediction models, software quality, software quality assurance, Software quality assurance, software systems complexity, trends and future directions","pages":"33--45"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"ma_empirical_2016","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"Empirical analysis of network measures for effort-aware fault-proneness prediction","volume":"69","issn":"0950-5849","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0950584915001524","doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.infsof.2015.09.001","abstract":"Context Recently, network measures have been proposed to predict fault-prone modules. Leveraging the dependency relationships between software entities, network measures describe the structural features of software systems. However, there is no consensus about their effectiveness for fault-proneness prediction. Specifically, the predictive ability of network measures in effort-aware context has not been addressed. Objective We aim to provide a comprehensive evaluation on the predictive effectiveness of network measures with the effort needed to inspect the code taken into consideration. Method We first constructed software source code networks of 11 open-source projects by extracting the data and call dependencies between modules. We then employed univariate logistic regression to investigate how each single network measure was correlated with fault-proneness. Finally, we built multivariate prediction models to examine the usefulness of network measures under three prediction settings: cross-validation, across-release, and inter-project predictions. In particular, we used the effort-aware performance indicators to compare their predictive ability against the commonly used code metrics in both ranking and classification scenarios. Results Based on the 11 open-source software systems, our results show that: (1) most network measures are significantly positively related to fault-proneness; (2) the performance of network measures varies under different prediction settings; (3) network measures have inconsistent effects on various projects. Conclusion Network measures are of practical value in the context of effort-aware fault-proneness prediction, but researchers and practitioners should be careful of choosing whether and when to use network measures in practice.","journal":"Information and Software Technology","author":"Ma, Wanwangying and Chen, Lin and Yang, Yibiao and Zhou, Yuming and Xu, Baowen","year":"2016","keywords":"Dependency relationships, Effort-aware, Fault-proneness prediction, Network measures","pages":"50 -- 70"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"martin_oo_1994","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"{OO} design quality metrics","author":"Martin, Robert","year":"1994"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"mccabe_complexity_1976","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"title":"