tive models, Software, software metrics, Measurement, public domain software, Training, ArgoUML, code metrics, cross project prediction, Eclipse, forward release prediction, Java, JRuby, network metrics, open source Java projects, open-source, replication study, software entities, software system, source code metrics, Windows Server 2003","pages":"215--224"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"qu_node2defect_2018","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"address":"New York, NY, USA","series":"{ASE} 2018","title":"Node2Defect: {Using} {Network} {Embedding} to {Improve} {Software} {Defect} {Prediction}","isbn":"978-1-4503-5937-5","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/3238147.3240469","doi":"10.1145/3238147.3240469","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 33rd {ACM}/{IEEE} {International} {Conference} on {Automated} {Software} {Engineering}","publisher":"ACM","author":"Qu, Yu and Liu, Ting and Chi, Jianlei and Jin, Yangxu and Cui, Di and He, Ancheng and Zheng, Qinghua","year":"2018","keywords":"defect prediction, software metrics, network embedding, Software defect","pages":"844--849"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"qu_using_2019","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"title":"Using {K}-core {Decomposition} on {Class} {Dependency} {Networks} to {Improve} {Bug} {Prediction} {Model}'s {Practical} {Performance}","issn":"0098-5589","doi":"10.1109/TSE.2019.2892959","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","author":"Qu, Y. and Zheng, Q. and Chi, J. and Jin, Y. and He, A. and Cui, D. and Zhang, H. and Liu, T.","year":"2019","keywords":"Predictive models, Software, Computer bugs, software defects, Bug prediction, class dependency network, complex network, Complex networks, effort-aware bug prediction, Mathematical model, Prediction algorithms, Software algorithms","pages":"1--1"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"schonemann_generalized_1966","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"title":"A generalized solution of the orthogonal procrustes problem","volume":"31","issn":"1860-0980","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02289451","doi":"10.1007/BF02289451","abstract":"A solutionT of the least-squares problemAT=B +E, givenA andB so that trace (E´xE)= minimum andT´xT=I is presented. It is compared with a less general solution of the same problem which was given by Green [5]. The present solution, in contrast to Green's, is applicable to matricesA andB which are of less than full column rank. Some technical suggestions for the numerical computation ofT and an illustrative example are given.","number":"1","journal":"Psychometrika","author":"Schönemann, Peter H.","month":"mar","year":"1966","pages":"1--10"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"shukla_multi-objective_2018","verdict":"partial","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"915aa24159699bb2","fields":{"title":"Multi-objective cross-version defect prediction","volume":"22","issn":"1433-7479","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00500-016-2456-8","doi":"10.1007/s00500-016-2456-8","abstract":"Defect prediction models help software project teams to spot defect-prone source files of software systems. Software project teams can prioritize and put up rigorous quality assurance (QA) activities on these predicted defect-prone files to minimize post-release defects so that quality software can be delivered. Cross-version defect prediction is building a prediction model from the previous version of a software project to predict defects in the current version. This is more practical than the other two ways of building models, i.e., cross-project prediction model and cross- validation prediction models, as previous version of same software project will have similar parameter distribution among files. In this paper, we formulate cross-version defect prediction problem as a multi-objective optimization problem with two objective functions: (a) maximizing recall by minimizing misclassification cost and (b) maximizing recall by minimizing cost of QA activities on defect prone files. The two multi-objective defect prediction models are compared with four traditional machine learning algorithms, namely logistic regression, naïve Bayes, decision tree and random forest. We have used 11 projects from the PROMISE repository consisting of a total of 41 different versions of these projects. Our findings show that multi-objective logistic regression is more cost-effective than single-objective algorithms.","number":"6","journal":"Soft Computing","author":"Shukla, Swapnil and Radhakrishnan, T. and Muthukumaran, K. and Neti, Lalita Bhanu Murthy","month":"mar","year":"2018","pages":"1959--1980"},"diffs":[{"field":"year","in_document":"2018","in_source":"2016","severity":"medium"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"smith_offline_2017","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"Offline bilingual word vectors, orthogonal transformations and the inverted softmax","volume":"abs/1702.03859","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03859","journal":"CoRR","author":"Smith, Samuel L. and Turban, David H. P. and Hamblin, Steven and Hammerla, Nils Y.","year":"2017"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"subelj_community_2011","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:29:51Z","response_hash":"c481e7bcb4a56af5","fields":{"title":"Community structure of complex software systems: {Analysis} and applications","volume":"abs/1105.4276","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.4276","journal":"CoRR","author":"Subelj, Lovro and Bajec, Marko","year":"2011"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-en